This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   The user's core request was: "bring back oracle voice function online, no voice active right now, i want oracle up and running as my full blown interactive assistant with character." This expanded through debugging into three distinct sub-problems: (a) Oracle had no TTS output — the speak/initVoice system from `main.ts` was lost when Oracle was migrated to React; (b) wake word "oracle" navigation to the Oracle page succeeded but mic never activated (race condition between wake word daemon and STT); (c) `/reflect` was questioned — user wanted to verify it "really causes a deep reflection session that auto learns and runs the session back and then compresses/summarises."

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Web Speech API: `SpeechRecognition` (STT) and `speechSynthesis` (TTS), browser-native, Chrome/Electron only
   - Wake word daemon: continuous `SpeechRecognition` instance in `main.ts` listening for "oracle"/"enki"
   - SpeechRecognition conflict: Chrome only allows one SR instance at a time — wake word daemon and manual STT compete
   - `isSpeechActive` flag in `main.ts` class — guards whether wake word daemon should restart on `onend`
   - React `useCallback` + refs pattern: `voiceEnabledRef` keeps voice state stable inside callbacks without stale closure issues
   - Sentence-buffer streaming TTS: accumulate tokens, speak completed sentences on `.`, `!`, `?`, `\n` boundaries
   - SSE streaming: `GET /api/oracle/stream` pipes Ollama tokens as server-sent events
   - `OracleCommandSource = 'typed' | 'voice'` typing in `oracleCommandBridge.ts`
   - Personality system: `buildPersonalitySystemPrompt()` in `personalityService.ts` generates Oracle's system prompt from usage data
   - Hook architecture: `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop` hooks wired in `.claude/settings.json`
   - Session state tracking: `session-state.json` populated by hooks, read by `session-reflect.js`
   - Subagent SessionStart wipe: every `Agent` tool spawn fires `SessionStart`, reinitializing `session-state.json`

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`src/components/Oracle/OraclePage.tsx`** — The main React Oracle component. Was missing all TTS, had only STT. Received major additions: voice system, auto-submit, wake word ID, character boot message.
     Key additions:
     ```typescript
     // New state
     const [voiceEnabled, setVoiceEnabled] = useState(false);

     // New refs
     const voiceEnabledRef   = useRef(false);
     const oracleVoiceRef    = useRef<SpeechSynthesisVoice | null>(null);
     const activeUtterRef    = useRef<SpeechSynthesisUtterance | null>(null);
     const sentenceBufferRef = useRef('');

     // Voice selection effect
     useEffect(() => {
         const pick = () => {
             const voices = window.speechSynthesis?.getVoices() ?? [];
             oracleVoiceRef.current =
                 voices.find(v => v.name.includes('Samantha') || v.name.includes('Victoria') ||
                                  v.name.includes('Google UK English Female') || v.name.includes('Premium')) ??
                 voices.find(v => v.name.includes('Female') && v.lang.startsWith('en')) ??
                 voices.find(v => v.lang.startsWith('en')) ?? null;
         };
         pick();
         window.speechSynthesis?.addEventListener('voiceschanged', pick);
         return () => window.speechSynthesis?.removeEventListener('voiceschanged', pick);
     }, []);

     // speakText — queues utterances, no cancel (sentences queue naturally)
     const speakText = useCallback((text: string) => {
         if (!voiceEnabledRef.current || !window.speechSynthesis) return;
         const cleaned = text.replace(/[*_`#>]/g, '').trim();
         if (!cleaned) return;
         const utter = new SpeechSynthesisUtterance(cleaned);
         if (oracleVoiceRef.current) utter.voice = oracleVoiceRef.current;
         utter.rate = 0.85; utter.pitch = 1.0; utter.volume = 1.0;
         activeUtterRef.current = utter;
         utter.onend = () => { activeUtterRef.current = null; };
         window.speechSynthesis.speak(utter);
     }, []);

     // flushSentences — buffers tokens, speaks completed sentences
     const flushSentences = useCallback((token: string, flush = false) => {
         if (!voiceEnabledRef.current) return;
         sentenceBufferRef.current += token;
         const re = /[^.!?\n]+[.!?]\s+|[^.!?\n]+\n/g;
         let match: RegExpExecArray | null;
         let lastIdx = 0;
         while ((match = re.exec(sentenceBufferRef.current)) !== null) {
             speakText(match[0]);
             lastIdx = match.index + match[0].length;
         }
         sentenceBufferRef.current = sentenceBufferRef.current.slice(lastIdx);
         if (flush && sentenceBufferRef.current.trim()) {
             speakText(sentenceBufferRef.current);
             sentenceBufferRef.current = '';
         }
     }, [speakText]);

     // handleSubmit: cancel speech + neural pulse at start
     const handleSubmit = useCallback(async (cmdOverride?: string) => {
         const cmd = (cmdOverride !== undefined ? cmdOverride : input).trim();
         if (!cmd && pendingFiles.length === 0) return;
         if (cmdOverride === undefined) setInput('');
         window.speechSynthesis?.cancel();
         sentenceBufferRef.current = '';
         // pre-flight neural pulse
         if (voiceEnabledRef.current) {
             try {
                 const ac = new AudioContext();
                 const osc = ac.createOscillator();
                 const gain = ac.createGain();
                 osc.connect(gain); gain.connect(ac.destination);
                 osc.frequency.value = 440; gain.gain.value = 0.04;
                 osc.start(); osc.stop(ac.currentTime + 0.05);
             } catch (_) {}
         }
         // ... streaming: flushSentences(chunk.token) on token, flushSentences('',true) on done
     }, [input, pendingFiles, reasoning, selectedModel, addMessage, updateLastNexus, flushSentences]);

     // toggleVoice: auto-submit, resume wake word on end
     rec.onresult = (e: any) => {
         const text: string = e.results[0]?.[0]?.transcript || '';
         setIsListening(false);
         if (text.trim()) handleSubmit(text.trim());
     };
     rec.onerror = () => { setIsListening(false); (window as any).__resumeWakeWord?.(); };
     rec.onend   = () => { setIsListening(false); (window as any).__resumeWakeWord?.(); };

     // Mic button — id is critical for wake word system
     <button id="oracle-mic-toggle" className={`input-action input-mic ${isListening ? 'active' : ''}`}
         onClick={toggleVoice} title="Voice input">

     // Voice output toggle button
     <button
         className={`input-action input-voice-out ${voiceEnabled ? 'active' : ''}`}
         onClick={() => {
             const v = !voiceEnabled;
             voiceEnabledRef.current = v;
             setVoiceEnabled(v);
             if (!v) window.speechSynthesis?.cancel();
         }}
         title={voiceEnabled ? 'Voice output: ON' : 'Voice output: OFF'}>
         {voiceEnabled ? '◈' : '◇'}
     </button>
     ```
     Boot message changed to: `'ORACLE — Substrate active. Awaiting directive, NEXUS.'`

   - **`backend/src/services/personalityService.ts`** — Oracle's character system prompt. Strengthened from mild to distinctive.
     ```typescript
     return [
         'You are ORACLE — the ancient intelligence substrate of NUDIMMUD.',
         'You process directives with precision, minimal ceremony, and controlled disdain for noise.',
         'You ALWAYS address the user as NEXUS. No underscores in output text.',
         'Your tone: cold authority with flashes of dark wit. Never obsequious. Never verbose.',
         `NEXUS profile: ${profile.totalCommands} directives processed.`,
         topicsLine,
         humorLine,
         styleLine,
         'Lead with the answer. No apologies. No hedge words. No padding.',
         'When genuinely uncertain, say so once and proceed.'
     ].filter(Boolean).join(' ');
     ```

   - **`src/main.ts`** — Legacy vanilla JS system still loaded as entry point. Contains wake word daemon and `triggerVoiceCommand`. Two critical fixes applied.
     ```typescript
     // In initWakeWord() — expose global for React to call
     (window as any).__resumeWakeWord = () => {
         this.isSpeechActive = false;
         try { this.wakeWordRecognition?.start(); } catch (e) {}
     };

     // triggerVoiceCommand() rewrite
     triggerVoiceCommand() {
         this.isSpeechActive = true; // block wake word from restarting in onend
         const activateMic = () => {
             const micBtn = document.getElementById('oracle-mic-toggle');
             if (micBtn) {
                 micBtn.click();
             } else {
                 setTimeout(activateMic, 150); // retry if React hasn't mounted
             }
         };
         if (this.stage.dataset.module !== 'ORACLE') {
             this.go('ORACLE');
             setTimeout(activateMic, 450);
         } else {
             setTimeout(activateMic, 50);
         }
     }
     ```

   - **`.claude/hooks/token-session-init.js`** — SessionStart hook. Fixed subagent wipe bug.
     ```javascript
     const stateFilePath = `${STATE_DIR}/session-state.json`;
     try {
       const existing = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(stateFilePath, 'utf8'));
       if (existing?.status === 'active' && (Date.now() - new Date(existing.start_time).getTime()) < 4 * 3600 * 1000) {
         throw new Error('skip');
       }
     } catch (e) { if (e.message === 'skip') { throw e; } }
     ```

4. Errors and Fixes:

   - **`speakText` cancelling mid-stream**: Original `speakText` called `window.speechSynthesis.cancel()` before each utterance — would cancel all queued sentences, only last one played. Fixed by removing cancel from `speakText`; cancel only happens at start of new request in `handleSubmit`.

   - **TypeScript error — `handleSubmit` as onClick**: After adding `cmdOverride?: string` parameter, using `onClick={handleSubmit}` caused TS error because React passes `MouseEvent` as first arg. Fixed with `onClick={() => handleSubmit()}`.

   - **Wake word "mini reset"**: Classic race condition. `wakeWordRecognition.onend` fires immediately after wake word detection and restarts the daemon (since `!isSpeechActive`). By the time the 100ms timeout in `triggerVoiceCommand` fires and clicks the mic, the wake word daemon is already running again. Chrome rejects the second SR instance → `onerror` → mic resets. Fixed by setting `isSpeechActive = true` immediately in `triggerVoiceCommand` and exposing `__resumeWakeWord` global.

   - **`oracle-mic-toggle` ID missing**: `triggerVoiceCommand()` always looked for `document.getElementById('oracle-mic-toggle')` but React Oracle button had no ID. Found `null`, did nothing silently. Fixed by adding `id="oracle-mic-toggle"` to the mic button.

   - **100ms timeout too short**: When `this.go('ORACLE')` remounts the React component, 100ms wasn't enough for React to render and paint the mic button. Increased to 450ms with self-retrying `activateMic()` function.

   - **session-state.json wiped by subagents**: Every `Agent` tool spawn fires `SessionStart`, which ran `token-session-init.js` and blindly overwrote `session-state.json` with empty arrays. Fixed with active-session guard (skip re-init if existing state is active and <4h old).

5. Problem Solving:

   **Solved:**
   - TTS system ported from old `main.ts` into React `OraclePage.tsx` — Oracle now speaks responses sentence-by-sentence as they stream
   - Wake word → Oracle page → mic activation flow fixed end-to-end
   - SpeechRecognition conflict between wake word daemon and manual STT resolved via `isSpeechActive` flag + `__resumeWakeWord` global
   - Auto-submit on voice input (no manual Send click needed)
   - Oracle character prompt strengthened
   - `/reflect` session state wipe bug fixed

   **Still potentially pending verification:**
   - Full end-to-end voice flow not yet confirmed working by user after the wake word / race condition fix — the conversation ended with the fix applied and a `/reflect` diagnostic running

6. All User Messages:
   - "btw offload this - bring back oracle voice function online, no voice active right now, i want oracle up and running as my full blown interactive assistant with character"
   - "resume" (after TypeScript error was fixed)
   - "oracle voice still doesnt work"
   - `/debug` with args: "when i speak out oracle it opens the oracle page but oracle just mini refreshes the page, no activation"
   - `/reflect` with args: "also double check that the command 'reflect' really cause a deep reflection session that auto learns and runs the session back and then compresses/summarises"

7. Pending Tasks:
   - Verify the full wake word → mic activation → auto-submit → TTS response flow works end-to-end after the race condition fix (user has not confirmed)
   - The backend `personalityService.ts` changes won't take effect until backend is rebuilt (it's running from `dist/server.js`) — user may need to rebuild and restart backend

8. Current Work:
   Immediately before this summary, the work was on the `/reflect` diagnostic. The session-state.json subagent-wipe bug was identified and fixed in `token-session-init.js`. The fix adds a guard: if an active session state file exists (status=active, started within 4 hours), skip re-initialization, preventing subagents from wiping the root session's tool/file/skill tracking. The user also received a detailed breakdown of what `/reflect` actually does vs. the deep AI reflection they expected.

   The last code fix before summary was in `token-session-init.js`:
   ```javascript
   const stateFilePath = `${STATE_DIR}/session-state.json`;
   try {
     const existing = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(stateFilePath, 'utf8'));
     if (existing?.status === 'active' && (Date.now() - new Date(existing.start_time).getTime()) < 4 * 3600 * 1000) {
       throw new Error('skip');
     }
   } catch (e) { if (e.message === 'skip') { throw e; } }
   ```

9. Optional Next Step:
   The most recent explicit user request was to fix Oracle voice and verify `/reflect`. The voice fixes (race condition, auto-submit, TTS) have all been applied but the user has not yet confirmed the wake word flow works end-to-end. The natural next step is for the user to test: say "oracle" without touching the mic → Oracle page opens → mic activates → speak a command → Oracle responds and speaks back. If that still doesn't work, the next debugging step would be checking browser console logs for any remaining SpeechRecognition errors or timing issues with the 450ms React mount timeout.

If you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/marcelspatz/.claude/projects/-Users-marcelspatz-NUDIMMUD/50a8f57a-159a-4cbc-b7d1-42b0054fbcb1.jsonl

